WEBVTT

00:01.426 --> 00:04.600
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.785 --> 00:07.793
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.861 --> 00:11.003
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.071 --> 00:14.414
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.481 --> 00:17.590
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.657 --> 00:21.535
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.604 --> 00:23.139
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.207 --> 00:24.477
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.546 --> 00:26.516
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:32.570 --> 00:34.040
<i>Hi. This is Peter.</i>

00:34.108 --> 00:35.745
<i>Don't get scared
that you can hear my voice</i>

00:35.812 --> 00:37.149
<i>but you can't see me.</i>

00:37.218 --> 00:39.288
<i>This is the story
of a great adventure</i>

00:39.357 --> 00:41.228
<i>that happened to me
and some of my pals.</i>

00:41.295 --> 00:43.335
<i>It all began innocently enough,</i>

00:43.403 --> 00:46.477
<i>with my stupid wife showing me
some dumb-ass brochure.</i>

00:46.546 --> 00:49.186
So, here's where we'll all
be staying this weekend.

00:49.254 --> 00:50.891
You and I will
have one cabin,

00:50.958 --> 00:52.295
and Bonnie and
Joe and Quagmire

00:52.363 --> 00:53.565
will have the
other two.

00:53.633 --> 00:55.439
Ah, this is going
to be so much fun!

00:56.710 --> 00:58.246
Hi, Chris.
How was school?

00:58.314 --> 00:59.450
Not good.

00:59.517 --> 01:01.858
I got suspended for
saying bad words.

01:01.926 --> 01:03.228
Oh, for God's sake!

01:03.296 --> 01:04.834
My principal wants to
meet with you guys.

01:04.901 --> 01:06.003
Should we go?

01:06.071 --> 01:07.308
It sounds like a trap.

01:07.375 --> 01:08.679
Yes, Peter,
we should go.

01:08.746 --> 01:11.120
All right, but if it's a trap
and we don't come back,

01:11.187 --> 01:12.556
I get to make
smart-alecky remarks

01:12.624 --> 01:14.997
when we're tied up back-to-back,
like last time.

01:15.065 --> 01:17.907
Any more bright
ideas, Professor?

01:21.216 --> 01:24.025
Mr. and Mrs. Griffin, the
reason Chris was suspended

01:24.093 --> 01:26.867
is that he told a very
inappropriate joke in class.

01:26.935 --> 01:28.104
Well, Principal Shepherd,

01:28.172 --> 01:30.076
we promise you
it won't happen again.

01:30.145 --> 01:31.982
I don't know where Chris
heard the joke,

01:32.050 --> 01:33.955
but I can assure you
it wasn't at home.

01:34.023 --> 01:35.192
Was it, Chris?

01:35.260 --> 01:36.897
No. Mr. Quagmire
told it to me.

01:36.965 --> 01:38.368
I should have figured.

01:38.436 --> 01:40.040
Was it the one
where the blind man

01:40.107 --> 01:42.548
walks by the fish market and
says, "Good morning, ladies"?

01:42.616 --> 01:44.420
(laughing):
I told you that one!

01:44.487 --> 01:45.724
You told me that one.

01:45.793 --> 01:47.062
I sure did.

01:47.129 --> 01:48.901
We enjoy
each other's company.

01:52.880 --> 01:54.116
Hey, Quagmire.

01:54.184 --> 01:55.787
You know, you got Chris
suspended from school

01:55.855 --> 01:57.125
for telling one of
your dirty jokes.

01:57.193 --> 01:58.429
Oh, gosh, Peter, I'm sorry.

01:58.498 --> 01:59.967
You want me to talk to him?

02:00.035 --> 02:01.071
Well, no,
actually, I...

02:01.139 --> 02:02.541
I want you to tell
me the joke.

02:02.609 --> 02:03.812
Yeah, tell us
the joke.

02:03.880 --> 02:05.317
You want to hear it?
All right.

02:05.385 --> 02:07.424
So, this chick meets a guy
at a bar, and...

02:07.492 --> 02:09.329
(muttering indistinctly)

02:10.869 --> 02:13.174
P.S. Your vagina's in the sink.

02:13.242 --> 02:16.050
(guffawing)

02:16.117 --> 02:18.022
Oh, God,
I pooped my pants.

02:18.090 --> 02:20.998
(chuckles) It's funny
when it happens to other people.

02:23.406 --> 02:26.081
Yuck. That's the end
of those underwears.

02:26.148 --> 02:28.253
I didn't know what to do,
so I took them off

02:28.321 --> 02:30.460
and hummed them at the wall,
and they started sliding down

02:30.527 --> 02:31.496
like one of them
sticky octopuses.

02:31.565 --> 02:32.667
Well, it's a pretty funny joke,

02:32.735 --> 02:33.870
you know,
when you think about it.

02:33.938 --> 02:35.208
"Your vagina's in the sink."

02:35.275 --> 02:36.979
(laughs)
Damn it!

02:38.352 --> 02:40.724
Wow. He poops every time
he hears that joke.

02:40.792 --> 02:42.096
(chuckles)
Yeah.

02:42.164 --> 02:44.035
He does, doesn't he?

02:47.212 --> 02:49.518
(both giggling)

02:49.585 --> 02:51.023
Get out of here,
Quagmire!

02:51.091 --> 02:52.828
I just put on
clean pants!

02:55.671 --> 02:57.609
(cell phone vibrating)
Who's texting me?

02:57.677 --> 02:59.414
(laughs)
Damn it!

02:59.483 --> 03:02.023
(Quagmire and Joe
laughing)

03:02.091 --> 03:03.360
Stop it, you guys!

03:03.428 --> 03:05.099
You're ruining all my clothes!

03:12.288 --> 03:14.360
Okay, Quagmire,
he's asleep.

03:25.562 --> 03:26.864
(laughing)

03:29.407 --> 03:30.442
Peter!

03:30.510 --> 03:32.115
You just pooped
all over the bed!

03:32.183 --> 03:36.259
When you poop in your dreams,
you poop for real.

03:40.373 --> 03:42.177
Hello, fellas.

03:42.246 --> 03:43.917
Hey, Pete...
Hey, those are my pants.

03:43.985 --> 03:45.187
That's right.
Thought I'd come by

03:45.255 --> 03:46.926
and see if you have
any jokes to tell.

03:46.994 --> 03:48.296
I enjoy a joke.

03:48.364 --> 03:49.634
I don't know.

03:49.702 --> 03:51.740
I want to tell the joke,
but I like those pants.

03:51.808 --> 03:52.944
I'll tell the joke.

03:53.012 --> 03:54.282
Go ahead, Joe. I'm all anus.

03:54.350 --> 03:55.518
Joe, don't you dare.

03:55.586 --> 03:56.723
I'll push you straight
into traffic.

03:56.790 --> 03:57.892
Peter, you win.

03:57.960 --> 03:59.564
All right, I won't
tell the joke anymore.

03:59.633 --> 04:01.068
You know, I-I got
to admit, Quagmire,

04:01.136 --> 04:02.439
despite all
the problems,

04:02.507 --> 04:03.877
that joke is
freaking hilarious.

04:03.945 --> 04:05.816
Where'd you hear it?
Bruce told it to me.

04:05.884 --> 04:07.120
No way Bruce came
up with that.

04:07.188 --> 04:08.357
Where'd he hear it?

04:08.425 --> 04:09.729
I don't know--
probably just around.

04:09.797 --> 04:12.202
I mean, where does any
dirty joke come from?

04:12.271 --> 04:13.439
Hey, you know,
Joe is right.

04:13.507 --> 04:14.610
There's a million
of them.

04:14.678 --> 04:16.082
They got to be coming
from somewhere.

04:16.150 --> 04:18.054
I mean, somebody's got to
be making these things up.

04:18.121 --> 04:19.458
Well, who?
I don't know.

04:19.526 --> 04:21.598
But haven't you ever
wanted to find out?

04:21.666 --> 04:24.038
Well, yeah, but how
would anyone do that?

04:24.106 --> 04:25.410
A quest, Joe.

04:25.478 --> 04:27.349
We go on a quest
to find the source

04:27.416 --> 04:28.720
of the world's dirty jokes.

04:28.788 --> 04:29.956
Who's with me?

04:30.024 --> 04:30.993
Well, I'm with you.

04:31.061 --> 04:32.330
Oh, what the hell? So am I.

04:33.736 --> 04:35.272
<i>PETER:
And so began our journey</i>

04:35.340 --> 04:36.978
<i>to find the splendid source</i>

04:37.046 --> 04:38.816
<i>of off-color humor
as we know it.</i>

04:38.884 --> 04:41.392
<i>Our first stop
was to see Bruce.</i>

04:41.458 --> 04:42.661
Oh, hey.

04:42.729 --> 04:44.100
What size shoes
is y'alls?

04:44.168 --> 04:45.470
Actually,
we're not here to bowl.

04:45.538 --> 04:46.775
We were wondering
where you heard

04:46.842 --> 04:48.446
that dirty joke
you told Quagmire.

04:48.514 --> 04:50.318
Oh, that one? Oh, no.

04:50.387 --> 04:52.759
I'm not going to tell y'all
that one here at the workplace.

04:52.827 --> 04:53.996
Too dirty.

04:54.063 --> 04:55.367
Maybe after quitting time,

04:55.435 --> 04:57.339
I'll have a mimosa
and tell y'all then.

04:57.407 --> 04:59.948
Look, you blade, just tell us
who you heard it from.

05:00.016 --> 05:02.522
<i>PETER:
It turned out the joke
already had quite a history.</i>

05:02.590 --> 05:04.260
<i>Bruce had heard it
from Consuela.</i>

05:04.328 --> 05:05.866
<i>Consuela heard it
from Mayor West.</i>

05:05.934 --> 05:07.337
<i>West heard it from Dr. Hartman.</i>

05:07.405 --> 05:09.009
<i>Hartman heard it from Angela,</i>

05:09.077 --> 05:11.216
<i>Angela from Opie,
Opie from Herbert.</i>

05:11.283 --> 05:12.687
<i>Herbert heard it
from Tom Tucker.</i>

05:12.753 --> 05:14.425
<i>Tucker heard it from Bender
on Futurama,</i>

05:14.493 --> 05:15.963
<i>oddly enough, for some reason.</i>

05:16.030 --> 05:17.267
<i>Bender heard it
from Al Harrington,</i>

05:17.335 --> 05:19.206
<i>Harrington from REO Speedwagon.</i>

05:19.274 --> 05:22.550
♪ Heard it from a friend who ♪

05:22.618 --> 05:25.192
♪ Heard it
from a friend who ♪

05:25.259 --> 05:27.265
♪ Heard it from another... ♪

05:27.332 --> 05:29.337
<i>REO Speedwagon
saved us several stops,</i>

05:29.405 --> 05:32.212
<i>as they, too, had backtracked
the joke to some extent.</i>

05:32.281 --> 05:33.717
<i>But when their trail had led</i>

05:33.785 --> 05:35.522
<i>to a bartender in Virginia,
they had given up,</i>

05:35.590 --> 05:37.663
<i>much the way the world
had given up on them.</i>

05:37.729 --> 05:39.903
<i>In fact, just to kick them
a couple extra bucks,</i>

05:39.971 --> 05:41.942
<i>here's five seconds
of "Time for Me to Fly."</i>

05:42.009 --> 05:43.179
No, don't!

05:43.247 --> 05:44.850
All the money goes
to my bitch ex-wife!

05:44.918 --> 05:46.423
Can you play our song?

05:46.490 --> 05:48.429
<i>PETER:
Okay, lead singer from Asia.</i>

05:48.496 --> 05:52.609
♪ Now, sure as the sun
will cross the sky ♪

05:52.676 --> 05:55.985
♪ This lie is over... ♪

05:59.329 --> 06:01.401
We can't go
to Virginia, Peter.

06:01.469 --> 06:03.775
Bonnie and Lois planned
that couples weekend to Maine.

06:03.843 --> 06:05.782
We're supposed to leave
in the morning.

06:05.850 --> 06:07.219
Yeah, Peter,
we've looked long enough.

06:07.286 --> 06:09.024
Maybe the joke
doesn't have a source.

06:09.091 --> 06:10.997
Don't be stupid.
Somebody had to have made it up.

06:11.065 --> 06:12.467
And we're going to find out who.

06:12.536 --> 06:13.973
Besides, this will be
way more fun

06:14.041 --> 06:15.811
than hanging out
in Maine with the wives,

06:15.879 --> 06:17.250
sitting around
a campfire,

06:17.317 --> 06:19.423
listening to Lois
tell grocery stories.

06:19.490 --> 06:22.532
(imitating Lois): "Oh, Peter,
you should have been there.

06:22.599 --> 06:25.340
"Uncle Ben's converted
brown rice was on sale.

06:25.408 --> 06:28.884
They marked it down
from $12 to... to three..."

06:28.952 --> 06:31.292
Whatever-- I don't know
how much rice is,

06:31.359 --> 06:32.663
but you know
what I'm saying.

06:39.218 --> 06:41.222
Okay, Peter,
I've got the directions.

06:41.290 --> 06:42.995
Head north
on the turnpike.

06:43.063 --> 06:44.967
That's going to be
the quickest route to Maine.

06:45.034 --> 06:46.204
Sure, Lois.

06:50.217 --> 06:52.725
Say, ladies, I was wondering
if you could tell me--

06:52.792 --> 06:54.429
what was childbirth like?

06:54.497 --> 06:56.836
Oh, Glenn, you
have no idea.

06:56.904 --> 06:59.177
It's something no man
could understand.

06:59.244 --> 07:02.854
Think of the most intense
pain you've ever felt,

07:02.923 --> 07:05.763
and imagine feeling
that for hours.

07:05.831 --> 07:07.368
<i>LOIS:
Well, and then,
by the eighth month,</i>

07:07.436 --> 07:10.110
<i>I had hemorrhoids that hung
like bunches of grapes.</i>

07:10.178 --> 07:13.588
<i>BONNIE:
And then, they said
I was four centimeters dilated.</i>

07:13.655 --> 07:15.559
They didn't think I was far
enough, but I was like,

07:15.628 --> 07:18.569
<i>"I can tell you
I'm far enough."</i>

07:18.637 --> 07:21.110
LOIS:
And that's when Chris was born.

07:21.178 --> 07:22.949
Gosh, that's all
so fascinating.

07:23.017 --> 07:24.487
Let me ask you
something else.

07:24.555 --> 07:26.861
Have you girls ever worked
in an office with other women

07:26.929 --> 07:28.834
who you have negative things
to say about?

07:28.902 --> 07:30.171
Oh, God, yes.
Oh, my God.

07:30.239 --> 07:31.441
Quagmire, shut up.
We're here.

07:33.590 --> 07:35.327
You drove us
to Virginia?!

07:35.416 --> 07:37.188
All right, look, we're sorry
we deceived you girls,

07:37.255 --> 07:38.592
but this is important.

07:38.660 --> 07:41.467
The trail leads to a bartender
who works here.

07:41.535 --> 07:43.907
He could be the source
of the dirty joke.

07:50.696 --> 07:53.403
Hi, there. What can I do
for you gentlemen?

07:53.471 --> 07:55.042
We've traveled a very long way

07:55.110 --> 07:56.914
to find out
where you heard this joke.

07:56.982 --> 07:59.255
Oh... (raspy laugh)

07:59.322 --> 08:00.960
I remember that.

08:01.028 --> 08:02.732
I heard it from that guy.

08:04.905 --> 08:05.774
Cleveland?!

08:05.842 --> 08:07.112
Hey, fellas.

08:07.179 --> 08:08.415
Holy crap!

08:08.483 --> 08:10.087
Who knew we'd run
into you here?

08:10.155 --> 08:12.395
Except everyone, if Fox
ruined it in the promos.

08:12.462 --> 08:14.300
What a surprise this is.

08:18.782 --> 08:21.488
Donna, it's so nice of you
to invite us to stay here.

08:21.556 --> 08:23.127
Oh, Lois,
it's my pleasure.

08:23.195 --> 08:25.768
I don't think we've seen
you folks since the wedding.

08:25.836 --> 08:27.306
Still waiting on that gift.

08:27.374 --> 08:29.780
The gift was the show.

08:29.848 --> 08:31.519
Uh, she doesn't know
what she's talking about.

08:31.587 --> 08:33.625
It's great to have
you-all down here.

08:33.693 --> 08:34.996
Hey, you know, Cleveland,
you better hide

08:35.064 --> 08:36.066
the markers from your kids.

08:36.134 --> 08:37.604
Somebody colored in your Jesus.

08:37.672 --> 08:40.748
Somebody colored in your ass
with too much ass, fat-ass.

08:40.815 --> 08:42.351
All right, Cleveland,
let's get down to business.

08:42.420 --> 08:43.823
Who told you the joke?

08:43.891 --> 08:47.267
A bellhop at the Royale
Hotel in Washington, DC.

08:47.335 --> 08:49.407
I met him when I took
Cleveland Jr. there

08:49.474 --> 08:51.246
to see the
Lincoln Memorial.

08:51.314 --> 08:54.221
But then Daddy got frustrated
'cause he couldn't find it,

08:54.290 --> 08:56.495
so we just ate fast food
in the parking lot.

08:56.563 --> 08:58.936
I'm just saying, maybe
put up a damn sign.

08:59.004 --> 09:01.710
Anyway, the bellhop's
name is Sal Russo.

09:01.778 --> 09:04.351
He knows every dirty
joke ever written.

09:04.420 --> 09:06.325
Then that's the guy
we got to talk to.

09:06.393 --> 09:08.866
Everyone, don't get too used
to being around black people,

09:08.934 --> 09:11.207
'cause we are going
to Washington, DC.

09:11.274 --> 09:12.811
Now, wait a minute, Peter.

09:12.880 --> 09:15.352
Donna's been nice enough to
invite us to stay the weekend,

09:15.421 --> 09:16.923
and frankly, that
sounds better

09:16.991 --> 09:18.762
than continuing this
wild-goose chase.

09:18.831 --> 09:21.136
Well, Lois, if you
and Bonnie want to stay here,

09:21.204 --> 09:22.942
maybe Cleveland could join us.

09:23.009 --> 09:24.347
Yeah, it'd be
just like old times.

09:24.414 --> 09:25.751
What do you say, Cleveland?

09:25.819 --> 09:27.021
Oh, I don't know.

09:27.089 --> 09:28.560
I've kind of got
my own life now.

09:28.628 --> 09:30.799
All right, well, if you
have a sudden change of heart

09:30.867 --> 09:32.604
and you want to chase us
down the street

09:32.672 --> 09:34.711
as we're pulling away,
you know where to find us.

09:34.779 --> 09:36.516
("What's Happening"
theme music playing)

09:47.985 --> 09:49.389
Okay, guys,
I got one.

09:49.457 --> 09:52.532
Would you rather get
a massage from a man

09:52.600 --> 09:55.106
or surgery from
a female doctor?

09:55.174 --> 09:56.077
Wow.

09:56.144 --> 09:57.447
Like, minor surgery?

09:57.514 --> 09:58.784
No, serious surgery.

09:58.852 --> 10:00.089
Like a blown kidney
or something.

10:00.156 --> 10:01.125
Geez.

10:01.193 --> 10:02.630
Good question, Peter.

10:02.697 --> 10:03.866
Is the man gay?
No.

10:03.934 --> 10:06.173
Is the female doctor
at least Jewish or Asian?

10:06.242 --> 10:07.478
No, but, actually,
you know what?

10:07.545 --> 10:09.149
I'm going to take
it up a notch.

10:09.218 --> 10:11.556
Hispanic female doctor
or gay male masseuse?

10:11.624 --> 10:13.361
Hispanic from Spain?

10:13.430 --> 10:14.800
No.

10:14.868 --> 10:16.170
Ah.
Ah.
Ah.

10:16.238 --> 10:17.642
So, it's basically--
would you rather

10:17.710 --> 10:19.848
get a massage from a gay man
or die?

10:19.916 --> 10:21.086
All right, I got
another one.

10:21.154 --> 10:22.957
Let Amy Winehouse
spit in your mouth

10:23.025 --> 10:25.565
or eat a raw slice of
Anderson Cooper's ass?

10:25.633 --> 10:27.605
Sign me up for Cooper.

10:27.673 --> 10:30.113
(gunshot blast, all scream)
What the hell?

10:30.181 --> 10:31.284
(tires screeching)

10:37.537 --> 10:38.973
(tires screeching)

10:43.489 --> 10:44.590
What the hell
was that about?

10:44.657 --> 10:45.727
Who were those guys?

10:45.795 --> 10:47.465
I don't know,
but I'll tell you this--

10:47.533 --> 10:50.242
I saw one of them
back in the bar in Stoolbend.

10:50.309 --> 10:51.779
You think they
wereollowing us?

10:51.846 --> 10:54.587
Either that or they got a grudge
against our back windshield.

10:54.655 --> 10:56.226
Ah, Joe, that's so dumb.

10:56.294 --> 10:58.064
Why would anybody
be trying to kill us?

10:58.132 --> 11:01.241
It might be safe to assume
that someone does not want us

11:01.309 --> 11:03.581
to learn the origin
of that joke.

11:03.649 --> 11:06.590
<i>PETER:
We had no idea how right
Cleveland was.</i>

11:06.658 --> 11:09.300
<i>And if we had known
what lay ahead,</i>

11:09.366 --> 11:10.837
<i>we would've stopped right there</i>

11:10.904 --> 11:12.275
<i>and gone straight back
to Quahog.</i>

11:12.343 --> 11:13.712
<i>But we didn't know.</i>

11:13.780 --> 11:14.983
<i>(whispers):
We didn't know.</i>

11:20.367 --> 11:22.772
There it is--
Washington, DC,

11:22.841 --> 11:24.211
the seat of government

11:24.279 --> 11:26.351
for the world's former
most powerful nation.

11:26.418 --> 11:28.992
Wow, those are all the monuments
I read about in school.

11:29.059 --> 11:30.329
There's the Washington Monument.

11:30.397 --> 11:34.676
There's the Obama Monument.

11:34.744 --> 11:36.782
And there's
the Vietnam War Memorial.

11:36.851 --> 11:38.888
Yeah, check out that Vietnamese
guy giving the business

11:38.957 --> 11:40.227
to those Vietnam Vets.

11:40.295 --> 11:43.369
Scoreboard!
Scoreboard!

11:43.437 --> 11:45.074
Aw, what happened
to your friend?!

11:45.142 --> 11:46.613
Hey, I know that guy!

11:46.681 --> 11:47.715
I kill him!

